# Scripts that run inside Linux containers must keep LF endings. Without this,
# a checkout or `git archive` on Windows (core.autocrlf=true) rewrites the
# shebang to "#!/bin/bash\r" and the container fails with
# "exec /entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory".
*.sh text eol=lf
entrypoint.sh text eol=lf
Start.bat text eol=crlf

# Same failure class as the *.sh rule above, one file this repo had missed
# (hunt-wave6-2026-08-29): a systemd unit file, always installed and parsed
# on the target Linux machine regardless of which OS checked it out. Copied
# verbatim by build.js (fs.copyFileSync, no normalization -- contrast with
# generateStartSh()'s explicit .replace(/\r\n/g, "\n") two lines above that
# copy) into every Linux release package. Without this rule, a Windows
# checkout (core.autocrlf=true) puts a trailing \r on every directive line;
# confirmed on this exact file in this exact repo, not assumed: `xxd` showed
# real 0d0a bytes on a Windows checkout before this rule existed. Only bites
# a LOCALLY-run `npm run build:exe:linux`/`node build.js --linux` on
# Windows -- release-artifacts.yml builds the Linux leg on ubuntu-22.04, so
# CI-published releases were never affected.
zomboid-panel.service text eol=lf
